Interpretation (for this tiny XOR run — do NOT generalise):
  sigmoid: derivatives peak at 0.25 and shrink fast when units saturate,
           so early gradients are small and convergence is slow.
  tanh:    zero-centred, derivative up to 1, usually trains faster than sigmoid.
  ReLU:    derivative is exactly 1 on the active side, 0 on the inactive side;
           larger early gradient, but if a unit starts inactive it can 'die'.
